  "notes": "{憎悪|ぞうお} is a formal, literary word expressing intense hatred or loathing—stronger than everyday words like {嫌|きら}い.\n\nUSAGE AS VERB:\n{憎悪|ぞうお}する: to hate intensely, to loathe\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}を{抱|いだ}く: to harbor hatred\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}に{満|み}ちた: filled with hatred\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}が{生|う}まれる: hatred arises\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {憎悪犯罪|ぞうおはんざい}: hate crime\n- {人種|じんしゅ}{憎悪|ぞうお}: racial hatred\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {憎悪|ぞうお}: intense hatred (formal, literary)\n- {憎|にく}む: to hate (neutral verb)\n- {嫌|きら}い: dislike (casual)\n- {恨|うら}み: grudge, resentment",
